				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thesmid" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2143744); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2143744&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607849607" alt="TheSMID" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2143744)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thesmid" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2143744); return false;" >TheSMID</a></span> <span class="odate time_1489000630 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Mar 2017 19:17</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2763114">
									

<p>I have just a few questions.</p>
<p>1.) How does one view the habits and mating of an 80,000 KM long entity? At the range required to be able to even see all of it, it would be far enough away you would using telescopes. That would be twice as long as this planet is AROUND.</p>
<p>2.) How does a creature that is 80,000 KM in length &quot;eat&quot; a living terrestrial organism? A person is ~2 meters tall, which means we're talking a &quot;mouth&quot; aperture (given the dimensions of snakes' mouths versus their bodies) at least 1000 KM wide. You could put something like 8 Death Stars in a mouth that big side-by-side and still have room left over. For this portal that is opened to be linked to or even in some way directed at the creature's mouth, the portal would have to be 1000 KM wide to direct mouth-sized food toward the creature. That's a very big hole to open between skip cells. Wouldn't any food sent through a portal just be floating through space toward a gaping maw for hours before that maw just&#8230; closes with it inside?</p>
<p>3.) How does a creature that is 80,000 KM long derive any energy whatsoever from something at most a few dozen meters in length, ala the largest terrestrial creatures on the planet assuming it can even get at those? (Whales and the like)</p>
<p>I don't mean these questions to be rude or anything. In fact, if they could be even addressed to some extent regarding the size of the creature, this could be a really great skip. I just find it very hard to get into the skip when it's so monstrously huge you can't even conceive of its size, but it eats people and somehow that's enough food for it?</p>

							</div>

								
					
